{%- import "_macros.j2" as labels -%}
  <!-- ========== TAB 7: MODEL EFFORT ========== -->
  <section class="tab-panel" id="model-effort" role="tabpanel" data-tab-title="Model Effort" x-show="tab==='model-effort'" x-cloak>
    <h2>Model Effort Analysis</h2>

    <p>Computational effort comparison across {{ total_models }} models{% if has_noplugin %} ({{ effort_data.models | length }} model/mode runs){% endif %} over {{ effort_data.fixtures | length - 1 }} test fixtures. Each cell shows the <strong>average</strong> value with a bar sized relative to the highest value in that column. The lighter bar extension shows how much worse the worst run was. Models are sorted by protocol compliance; <strong>click any column header to re-sort</strong>. Hover a cell for exact min/avg/max values.</p>

    <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:-0.5rem;">
      Model names are abbreviated (<code>claude-</code> / <code>openai-</code> prefixes removed). Models evaluated <strong>without</strong> the plugin carry a {{ labels.no_plugin_pill() }} badge in tables and a trailing asterisk (<code>*</code>) in charts.
    </p>

    <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:0.75rem; margin:1.5rem 0 0.5rem;">
      <label for="effort-fixture-select" style="font-weight:600; font-size:0.85rem; white-space:nowrap;">Fixture:</label>
      <select id="effort-fixture-select"
              aria-label="Select fixture for effort charts"
              style="font-size:0.85rem; padding:0.35rem 0.75rem; border-radius:6px; border:1px solid var(--border); background:var(--surface); color:var(--text); min-width:260px; cursor:pointer;">
        {% for fixture_id, fixture_label in effort_data.fixture_items %}
        <option value="{{ fixture_id }}">{{ fixture_label }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
      <table id="effort-table" class="data-table sortable-table compact" data-sort-fallback="3:asc,6:asc,0:asc" aria-label="Model effort metrics: tokens, elapsed time, and turns per model">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Model</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="min-width:92px;">Run Date</th>
            <th class="sorted-desc" data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:right; min-width:80px;">Pass Rate</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Input Tokens</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Output Tokens</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Elapsed Time</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:left; min-width:130px;">Turns</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for model in effort_data.models %}
          {% set agg = effort_data.by_fixture['__aggregate__'][model] %}
          {% set pr = effort_data.pass_rates[model] %}
          <tr data-model="{{ model }}"
              data-model-mode="{{ model_modes[model] | default('plugin') }}"
              data-pass="{{ pr }}"{% if model in effort_data.nodata_models %} class="row-nodata"{% endif %}>
            <td class="col-model" style="text-align:left;">{{ labels.model_label(model, abbreviate=true) }}{% if model_modes[model] | default('plugin') != 'plugin' %} {{ labels.no_plugin_pill() }}{% endif %}</td>
            <td>{{ model_run_dates[model] | default("&mdash;" | safe, true) }}</td>
            <td class="col-num" style="text-align:right;">{% if pr >= 95 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green); font-weight:600;">{{ pr }}%</span>{% elif pr >= 85 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">{{ pr }}%</span>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-red);">{{ pr }}%</span>{% endif %}</td>
            {% for metric in ['input_tokens', 'output_tokens', 'elapsed_s', 'turns'] %}
            {% set s = agg[metric] %}
            <td class="col-bar" data-metric="{{ metric }}" data-avg="{{ s.avg_val }}" data-min="{{ s.min_val }}" data-max="{{ s.max_val }}" data-sort-value="{{ s.avg_val }}">
              <span class="bar-label">{{ s.avg_val | round(1) }}</span>
            </td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:0.8rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:0.6rem; display:flex; gap:1.25rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <span><span class="legend-swatch legend-primary"></span> Average</span>
      <span><span class="legend-swatch legend-extent"></span> Max spread (less = more consistent)</span>
    </p>

    <!-- ── Pareto Frontier ── -->
    <h3 style="margin-top:2rem;">Cost vs Quality</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
      Each point is a model. The <strong style="color:var(--sf-green);">green frontier</strong> marks the optimal trade-off set - among models meeting the {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}% quality bar, no other is both cheaper <em>and</em> more accurate. Grey points meet the {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}% threshold but are not on the frontier. <span style="color:var(--sf-red);">Red triangles</span> fall below the {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}% threshold and are excluded from both the frontier and the efficiency rankings - a model that skips this much of the protocol is not a rational choice at any price.
    </p>
    <div class="chart-container" style="background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px; padding:1rem; height:520px;">
      <div id="effort-pareto-chart"
              aria-label="Scatter plot showing cost vs quality Pareto frontier"
              role="img"
              style="display:block; width:100%; height:480px;"></div>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin:0.9rem 0 0.5rem;">
      The same data as an exact lookup, cheapest first. <strong>Click any column header to re-sort.</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table id="pareto-table" class="data-table sortable-table compact" data-sort-fallback="3:desc,1:asc" aria-label="Cost versus quality ranking per model">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="col-rank" style="text-align:right; min-width:44px;">#</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Model</th>
            <th class="sorted-asc" data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:right; min-width:120px;">Avg Total Tokens</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:right; min-width:90px;">Pass Rate</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="text-align:left; min-width:150px;">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for p in effort_data.pareto_data | sort(attribute='avg_total_tokens') %}
          <tr data-model="{{ p.model }}"
              data-model-mode="{{ model_modes[p.model] | default('plugin') }}"
              data-tokens="{{ p.avg_total_tokens }}"
              data-pass="{{ p.pass_rate }}"
              data-status="{% if p.below_threshold %}3-below{% elif p.on_frontier %}1-frontier{% else %}2-off{% endif %}">
            <td class="col-rank" style="text-align:right; color:var(--text-muted);">{{ loop.index }}</td>
            <td class="col-model" style="text-align:left;">{{ labels.model_label(p.model, abbreviate=true) }}{% if model_modes[p.model] | default('plugin') != 'plugin' %} {{ labels.no_plugin_pill() }}{% endif %}</td>
            <td style="text-align:right; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;">{{ '{:,}'.format(p.avg_total_tokens | round | int) }}</td>
            <td style="text-align:right; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;">
              {% if p.pass_rate >= 95 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green); font-weight:600;">{{ p.pass_rate }}%</span>
              {% elif p.pass_rate >= 85 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">{{ p.pass_rate }}%</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-red);">{{ p.pass_rate }}%</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="text-align:left; font-size:0.8rem;">
              {% if p.below_threshold %}<span style="color:var(--sf-red);">&#9651; Below {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}%</span>
              {% elif p.on_frontier %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green);">&#9679; On frontier</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--text-muted);">&#9679; Off frontier</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Stochastic Reliability ── -->
    <h3 style="margin-top:2rem;">Stochastic Reliability</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
      <strong>Token CV</strong> (coefficient of variation = std_dev ÷ mean) measures run-to-run token predictability - lower is more predictable.
      <strong>Flaky fixtures</strong> are fixtures where pass/fail outcomes varied across runs; a high flake count indicates unstable protocol adherence.
      {% if effort_data.below_threshold %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">Models below the {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}% threshold are shown separately and excluded from efficiency rankings.</span>{% endif %}
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data-table sortable-table compact" data-sort-fallback="2:asc,3:asc,0:asc" aria-label="Stochastic reliability metrics per model">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="text-align:left;">Model</th>
            <th class="sorted-desc" data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:center;">Pass Rate</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:center;">Token CV</th>
            <th data-sort-type="number" style="text-align:center;">Flaky Fixtures</th>
            <th data-sort-type="text" style="text-align:center;">In Rankings?</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for model in effort_data.models %}
          {% set rel = effort_data.reliability_data[model] %}
          {% set pr  = effort_data.pass_rates[model] %}
          {% set above = model in effort_data.above_threshold %}
          <tr data-model-mode="{{ model_modes[model] | default('plugin') }}"{% if not above %} style="opacity:0.65;"{% endif %}>
            <td style="text-align:left; font-family:'SF Mono',monospace; font-size:0.8rem; font-weight:500;">{{ labels.model_label(model) }}{% if model_modes[model] | default('plugin') != 'plugin' %} {{ labels.no_plugin_pill() }}{% endif %}</td>
            <td style="text-align:center;">
              {% if pr >= 95 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green); font-weight:600;">{{ pr }}%</span>
              {% elif pr >= 85 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">{{ pr }}%</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-red);">{{ pr }}%</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="text-align:center; font-size:0.85rem;">
              {% if rel.token_cv == 0 %}<span style="color:var(--text-muted);"> - </span>
              {% elif rel.token_cv < 0.1 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green);">{{ rel.token_cv }}</span>
              {% elif rel.token_cv < 0.25 %}<span>{{ rel.token_cv }}</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">{{ rel.token_cv }}</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="text-align:center; font-size:0.85rem;">
              {% if rel.flaky_count == 0 %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green);">0</span>
              {% elif rel.flaky_count <= 2 %}<span>{{ rel.flaky_count }}</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-amber);">{{ rel.flaky_count }}</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">
              {% if above %}<span style="color:var(--sf-green);">&#10003; Yes</span>
              {% else %}<span style="color:var(--sf-red);">&#10007; Below {{ effort_data.quality_threshold }}% threshold</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
